---
title: "auctionLifecycle (LegionSealedBidAuctionSale)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_active: initialize() with ECIES publicKey
    q_active --> q_refund: block.timestamp >= endTime
    q_refund --> q_init_results: initializePublishSaleResults() [locks cancellation]
    q_init_results --> q_published: publishSaleResults() [releases privateKey]
    q_published --> q_supplied: supplyTokens()
    q_supplied --> q_distribution: investors claimTokenAllocation()
    q_distribution --> [*]: all investors claimed

    q_active --> q_canceled: cancel() by projectAdmin
    q_refund --> q_canceled: cancel() by projectAdmin (if !cancelLocked)
    q_canceled --> [*]: withdrawInvestedCapitalIfCanceled()

    note right of q_active
        INV-001: Active sale: encrypted bids via ECIES
        INV-002: Bid privacy preserved until privateKey release
    end note

    note right of q_init_results
        INV-003: Two-phase result publication prevents cancel after commitment
        INV-004: Private key release enables public bid verification
        INV-005: decryptSealedBid() available after publication
    end note

    note right of q_canceled
        INV-006: Cancel only possible before initializePublishSaleResults
        INV-007: Encrypted bids remain private if auction canceled
    end note
